for the bear.

1614
01:09:31,929 --> 01:09:33,895
-We'd better get out of here.
-"I'm out of here."

1615
01:09:39,378 --> 01:09:41,171
-That was a close shave.

1616
01:09:41,205 --> 01:09:43,481
-Well, we're not through yet.

1617
01:09:43,515 --> 01:09:45,378
[Whirring]

1618
01:09:54,067 --> 01:09:57,171
-Oh, Joel, it was so horrifying!

1619
01:09:57,205 --> 01:09:59,309
-Yeah? Really?
You think so?

1620
01:09:59,343 --> 01:10:01,791
-So ugly, so hideous!

1621
01:10:01,826 --> 01:10:04,102
-Uh, yeah, that was some eye,
wasn't it?

1622
01:10:04,136 --> 01:10:05,171
-No, not the eye.

1623
01:10:05,205 --> 01:10:06,550
We're talking about
Forrest Tucker.

1624
01:10:06,584 --> 01:10:09,722
-Oh, yeah, all that Vitalis,
those prop glasses,

1625
01:10:09,757 --> 01:10:11,240
and those heavy...

1626
01:10:11,274 --> 01:10:12,584
dramatic...

1627
01:10:12,619 --> 01:10:13,653
pauses.

1628
01:10:13,688 --> 01:10:15,446
I'm drained.
-No, you guys.

1629
01:10:15,481 --> 01:10:16,895
No, you got it wrong.

1630
01:10:16,929 --> 01:10:19,171
You see, the eye is what's
horrible about this movie.

1631
01:10:19,205 --> 01:10:20,205
Think about it.

1632
01:10:20,240 --> 01:10:21,274
Otherwise,
it would've been called

1633
01:10:21,309 --> 01:10:22,791
"The Crawling Forrest Tucker."

1634
01:10:22,826 --> 01:10:24,033
-I guess.

1635
01:10:24,067 --> 01:10:26,791
Joel, what's so scary
about a big eye, anyway?

1636
01:10:26,826 --> 01:10:27,998
-Oh, I see.

1637
01:10:28,033 --> 01:10:29,688
Well, it's another
human-being thing.

1638
01:10:29,722 --> 01:10:31,860
You know, anytime
we're confronted with some,

1639
01:10:31,895 --> 01:10:33,481
uh, appendage of ours

1640
01:10:33,515 --> 01:10:36,550
that's disconnected
and free-roaming, rogue,

1641
01:10:36,584 --> 01:10:40,033
you know, genetically bloated
to 10 times its normal size,

1642
01:10:40,067 --> 01:10:41,412
we're automatically scared.

1643
01:10:41,446 --> 01:10:43,584
-Especially if they
run in packs.

1644
01:10:43,619 --> 01:10:45,033
-I know what you mean.

1645
01:10:45,067 --> 01:10:48,343
Once, I got hassled by a pack ofreally tough pituitary glands.

1646
01:10:48,378 --> 01:10:50,309
And you know
how immature they can be.

1647
01:10:50,343 --> 01:10:52,171
-I still don't see why
it's so scary.

1648
01:10:52,205 --> 01:10:54,412
You could just walk up to it
and throw salt at it.

1649
01:10:54,446 --> 01:10:56,171
-Or just a squeeze
of lemon juice.

1650
01:10:56,205 --> 01:10:57,653
-Right, I know.

1651
01:10:57,688 --> 01:10:59,481
It's kind of a plot hole,
but let's kind of look it over.

1652
01:10:59,515 --> 01:11:01,826
You see, these --
Okay, these giant eyes

1653
01:11:01,860 --> 01:11:05,205
come from a world that's
designed for them, you know?

1654
01:11:05,240 --> 01:11:06,722
It's completely compatible.

1655
01:11:06,757 --> 01:11:10,446
Like, their highways are made
out of Nerf, and, uh --

1656
01:11:10,481 --> 01:11:12,550
and they don't have to
take shop classes.

1657
01:11:12,584 --> 01:11:15,240
-And they only use baby shampoo?-Right.

1658
01:11:15,274 --> 01:11:16,412
Right, exactly.

1659
01:11:16,446 --> 01:11:18,205
So, anyway, they come down
from this planet,

1660
01:11:18,240 --> 01:11:20,274
and they decide to land
on a mountain peak.

1661
01:11:20,309 --> 01:11:22,619
-Which is really stupid,
'cause as we all know,

1662
01:11:22,653 --> 01:11:25,998
a giant sharp point
is a giant eye's natural enemy.

1663
01:11:26,033 --> 01:11:29,067
-Bingo.
So, anyway, they come down,

1664
01:11:29,102 --> 01:11:31,964
and they fouled up
their atmosphere somehow.

1665
01:11:31,998 --> 01:11:33,102
I don't know.

1666
01:11:33,136 --> 01:11:34,378
It's hay fever season
or something.

1667
01:11:34,412 --> 01:11:35,998
And they figure they'd come downto Earth,

1668
01:11:36,033 --> 01:11:38,412
we'll have our first
frost already done with.

1669
01:11:38,446 --> 01:11:40,791
So, they come down,
and they have no concept

1670
01:11:40,826 --> 01:11:43,136
of anything at all,
like wearing safety glasses

1671
01:11:43,171 --> 01:11:45,343
or protective eyewear
of any kind.

1672
01:11:45,378 --> 01:11:47,136
-Joel, I think we've already
spent more time

1673
01:11:47,171 --> 01:11:50,446
examining this plot
than the writers ever did.

1674
01:11:50,481 --> 01:11:52,929
-Now here's something
you'll really like.

1675
01:11:52,964 --> 01:11:57,619
[Theme music playing]

1676
01:12:02,550 --> 01:12:06,412
-This is the last time.
-Put me down.

1677
01:12:06,446 --> 01:12:13,481
[Whirring]

1678
01:12:13,515 --> 01:12:16,412
-As a fog emerges
over Trollenberg,

1679
01:12:16,446 --> 01:12:19,343
our young group escapes.

1680
01:12:19,378 --> 01:12:22,895
-Looks like everything's
free and clear now.

1681
01:12:22,929 --> 01:12:24,067
Nothing to do but...

1682
01:12:24,102 --> 01:12:25,412
-Remember that telephone wire
to the hut?

1683
01:12:25,446 --> 01:12:26,826
-...get up the rope.

1684
01:12:26,860 --> 01:12:28,653
-Sit back and relax.

1685
01:12:28,688 --> 01:12:32,240
Enjoy the ride.

1686
01:12:32,274 --> 01:12:34,412
Uh-oh.

1687
01:12:34,446 --> 01:12:37,102
Maybe we spoke too soon.

1688
01:12:37,136 --> 01:12:38,619
-Oh, now they're gonna have
to wait all day

1689
01:12:38,653 --> 01:12:40,757
for that cable guy to show up.

1690
01:12:40,791 --> 01:12:42,688
-This contraption operate
in extreme cold?

1691
01:12:42,722 --> 01:12:44,550
-We've worked the cable car
in 30-below.

1692
01:12:44,584 --> 01:12:47,067
-Colder than that?
-Colder than a winch.

1693
01:12:49,826 --> 01:12:54,343
-Tell scary stories.
-Oh, my.

1694
01:12:54,378 --> 01:12:56,929
-The cable!
It will snap!

1695
01:13:04,653 --> 01:13:07,860
-"Am I gonna have time to changemy pants when I get there?"

1696
01:13:07,895 --> 01:13:09,550
-Oh, funny.
Good one.

1697
01:13:15,240 --> 01:13:18,067
Tell them all about
the giant eye, Forrest.

1698
01:13:18,102 --> 01:13:19,791
-All right, look, everybody out.

1699
01:13:22,826 --> 01:13:24,446
That's it.

1700
01:13:35,343 --> 01:13:36,860
-We're leaving the villagers
out here, sir.

1701
01:13:36,895 --> 01:13:38,895
It's shut and safe,
and they won't get in the way.

1702
01:13:38,929 --> 01:13:39,964
-The radio still working?

1703
01:13:39,998 --> 01:13:42,619
-We tested it about
15 minutes ago.

1704
01:13:42,653 --> 01:13:47,205
-Alan, come here.
Alan, we're in big trouble.

1705
01:13:47,240 --> 01:13:49,481
-What now?
-The cloud is splitting up.

1706
01:13:49,515 --> 01:13:51,481
-Splitting up?

1707
01:13:51,515 --> 01:13:55,412
-There are four of them now
and all moving this way.

1708
01:13:55,446 --> 01:13:57,412
-Four eyes.
-How long before they get here?

1709
01:13:57,446 --> 01:13:58,929
-An hour maybe.

1710
01:13:58,964 --> 01:14:01,412
-Well, that gives us an hour
to decide what we're gonna do.

1711
01:14:01,446 --> 01:14:02,998
Better check that radio again.

1712
01:14:03,033 --> 01:14:04,309
-You're going to signal
the authorities?

1713
01:14:04,343 --> 01:14:05,446
-And tell them what?

1714
01:14:05,481 --> 01:14:07,343
What do you use
against these things?

1715
01:14:07,378 --> 01:14:08,998
-High explosives.
-Bombs?

1716
01:14:09,033 --> 01:14:10,584
The time the plane gets here,

1717
01:14:10,619 --> 01:14:11,757
those things will be
all over us.

1718
01:14:11,791 --> 01:14:13,550
How do they drop
their bombs then?

1719
01:14:13,584 --> 01:14:15,722
-Set's still working okay, sir,
-Good.

1720
01:14:15,757 --> 01:14:18,412
Let me see that thing again.

1721
01:14:18,446 --> 01:14:21,343
-There's someone knockingat the outside door, Herr Wilde.

1722
01:14:25,102 --> 01:14:27,136
-It's Bob Hope.
-"Hey, there.

1723
01:14:27,171 --> 01:14:30,791
Join me this week with Brooke
Shields and Erik Estrada.

1724
01:14:30,826 --> 01:14:33,343
-He's doing a walk-on
in this movie.

1725
01:14:33,378 --> 01:14:36,515
-Is that a good Bob Hope, Joel?

1726
01:14:36,550 --> 01:14:39,033
-Well, we don't make up
our minds pretty soon,

1727
01:14:39,067 --> 01:14:42,757
they'll be made up for us.

1728
01:14:42,791 --> 01:14:46,757
-What does he mean by that?
-What's the matter?

1729
01:14:46,791 --> 01:14:48,895
What happened?
-He looks plastered.

1730
01:14:48,929 --> 01:14:50,688
